/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 526.9608661417322537 Td
(The terminal descent phase of lunar soft landing presents severe autonomous navigational challenges, as) Tj
T* (demonstrated during the Chandrayaan-2 Vikram descent where terminal guidance limitations and unexpected) Tj
T* (surface slopes impaired the landing trajectory. While Chandrayaan-3 achieved historic success at Shiv Shakti) Tj
T* (Point with an enlarged 4.0 km × 2.4 km target ellipse and the upgraded Lander Hazard Detection & Avoidance) Tj
T* (Camera \(LHDAC\), future lunar south pole missions targeting permanently shadowed regions \(PSRs\) require) Tj
T* (automated, real-time, deterministic hazard classification across extreme topographical gradients. LunarSafe) Tj
T* (provides an end-to-end deterministic hazard mapping pipeline that eliminates stochastic variances and) Tj
T* (guarantees identical hazard classifications across heterogeneous mission compute environments.) Tj
ET
